  "notes": "Family facts from the vendor installation manual (https://www.doc.hirschmann.com/pdf/IG_RS20_RS30_RS40_Managed_08_0325_en_2025-03-27.pdf): an RS30 has two gigabit uplink ports ('Ports 1 and 2, 1000 Mbit/s, media selectable, SFP, RJ45') beside 8, 16 or 24 10/100 Mbit/s TP RJ45 ports. The V.24 management connection is an RJ11 socket and the separate USB port is only for the ACA21-USB auto-configuration adapter, so neither is a data port. Power 12/24/48 V DC (9.6-60 V) or 24 V AC (18-30 V) on a redundant 6-pin terminal block. Temperature class letter in the code: S = standard 0 to +60 C, T and E = extended -40 to +70 C. Software variant letter: E = Layer 2 Enhanced, P = Professional. Layer 2 only: Belden lists switching, redundancy and management, never routing, so these specs carry no l3-forward. The manual numbers the front panel 1 to 26 for the 24-port RS30 ('Figure 8: Device variants with 2 x 1000 Mbit/s ports and 24 x 10/100 Mbit/s ports (RS30-2402...)'), which is why the two gigabit uplinks are Port 25 and Port 26 here. Datasheet: https://catalog.belden.com/techdata/EN/RS30-2402T1T1SDAE_techdata.pdf"
